WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.300
MEMORY UNITS

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:06.950
Data stored in the memory is measured in the units such as bits,

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:11.250
bytes, kilobytes, megabytes, gigabytes, terabytes and petabytes.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.250
Bit: A bit (short for binary digit) is the smallest unit of data in a computer.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.725
A bit has a single binary value, either 0 or 1.

00:00:23.575 --> 00:00:26.150
Byte: Combination of 8 bits.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.475
One byte stores one character such as any letter 'k',

00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:33.400
'a' or any other symbol like @, $, etc.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.675
Nibble

00:00:37.025 --> 00:00:39.775
Half a byte (four bits) is called Nibble.

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:45.875
The bits in a byte are normally numbered from zero to seven using the convention as

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:46.775
shown below :

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:50.975
MEASURING THE COMPUTER'S MEMORY

00:00:51.325 --> 00:00:54.225
One file can be of thousands of bytes.

00:00:54.575 --> 00:00:57.563
So, instead of using bytes to measure data,

00:00:57.563 --> 00:01:00.829
we can also use higher units such as kilobytes,

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:04.025
megabytes, gigabytes, terabytes and petabytes.

00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:08.850
Both computer memory and disk space are measured in these units.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:14.275
1 Bit = Binary Digit (0 or 1)

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:16.900
1 Byte = 8 Bits

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.325
1024 Bytes = 1 Kilo Byte

00:01:21.675 --> 00:01:26.675
1024 Kilo Bytes (KB) = 1 Mega Byte

00:01:27.025 --> 00:01:31.650
1024 Mega Bytes (MB) = 1 Giga Byte

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:38.575
1024 Giga Bytes (GB) = 1 Tera Byte

00:01:38.925 --> 00:01:43.900
1024 Tera Bytes (TB) = 1 Peta Byte

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:49.200
1024 Peta Bytes (PB) = 1 Exa Byte

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:54.475
1024 Exa Bytes (EB) = 1 Zetta Byte

00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:59.850
1024 Zetta Bytes (ZB) = 1 Yotta Byte
